# Vercel builds the Next.js radar in web/ and nothing else.
#
# Without this, Vercel scans the repo root, finds pyproject.toml, and offers to
# deploy spy_der/app/api.py as a serverless FastAPI function. That app must
# never be deployed here: it exposes unauthenticated mutating routes, including
# POST /risk/kill-switch?enabled=false, which would put a public reset for a
# latched kill switch on the internet. It is also stateful by design — the
# pipeline carries the HMM belief, the flow and wall trackers and the open book
# — so a serverless runtime would discard all of it on every cold start.
#
# The engine belongs on the dedicated CPU VPS behind loopback. See
# deploy/CPU_VPS.md.

spy_der/
scripts/
tests/
deploy/
docs/
pyproject.toml
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile*
*.db
.github/
